  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>One thing to know first</h2>
      <p>According to the FAQ of the Le Lavandou tourist office, access to the beaches is banned to dogs, even on a lead, from 1 April to 31 October (assistance dogs excepted). The campsites in the area, on the other hand, accept animals, under conditions that vary from one site to another.</p>

      <h2>What the tourist office pages say</h2>
      <p>The tourist office lists seven campsites in Le Lavandou and Bormes-les-Mimosas that accept animals. Examples of published conditions:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Camping Saint-Pons (3 stars, Le Lavandou)</strong>: animals accepted with a supplement, amount not published by the office; open from 18/04 to 04/10.</li>
        <li><strong>Camping Le Grand Batailler (2 stars, Bormes-les-Mimosas)</strong>: animals accepted, €3 per night; open from 15/05 to 15/10.</li>
        <li><strong>Camping Les Citronniers (2 stars, Le Lavandou)</strong>: animals accepted on a lead, including in the rentals; open from 01/05 to 30/09.</li>
        <li><strong>Camp du Domaine (Bormes-les-Mimosas)</strong>: dogs allowed on the grounds during the season, but not in the rentals, except the "Sunny" and "Rêve 5 pers." accommodations.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Where your dog can burn off energy</h2>
      <p>The "Caniludique du Grand Jardin" dog park, avenue de la Grande Bastide, offers 6,000 m² of free space with an agility course, free of charge, from 8:30 am to 8 pm (shorter hours on some days, for example 8:30 am-6 pm on Sunday 1 November 2026). Dogs must be identified, vaccinated, dewormed, treated against fleas and ticks, and stay under their owner's supervision.</p>

      <h2>To check before you book</h2>
      <p>Conditions vary by campsite and by type of accommodation (pitch or rental): confirm by phone the supplement, the number of dogs and the rentals concerned. For swimming, Bormes-les-Mimosas (tolerated zone near Fort de Brégançon) and Cavalaire-sur-Mer are cited in the previous version of this page, as is the coastal path between Le Lavandou and Cavalière being walkable on a lead all year round: these two points were not rechecked against an official source on 08/11/2026.</p>
    </div>

